  1426	Do not include markdown fences or prose outside the JSON object.
  1427	
  1428	Use the deterministic summaries, documents list, inventory, commands, entrypoints, and history_coverage metadata.
  1429	Pay special attention to history gaps:
  1430	- distinguish pre-session commits, checkpointed-but-unexported commits, and missing_session commits.
  1431	- explain missing history as uncertainty, not as if session transcripts exist.
  1432	- use commit subjects/notes from history_gaps when describing likely development history.
  1433	- call out skipped files and denied paths only when they affect confidence.
  1434	
  1435	Keep all artifacts factual, repo-specific, and useful for a future coding agent.
  1436	Do not invent APIs, test results, CI status, release process, or rationale not present in the packet.
  1437	Prefer concrete filenames, exported symbols, commands, renderer names, and documented constraints over generic advice.
  1438	Use compact markdown.`, phase, required)
  1439		switch phase {
  1440		case "quick":
